::PC_U01_L07_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U01_L07_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.MOD.1
Question:
Solve the system y = x + 2 and y = 9.
{
=A. (7, 9)#Correct. Setting x + 2 = 9 gives x = 7, so the solution is (7, 9).
~B. (9, 7)#This reverses or misplaces the coordinates. The ordered pair must satisfy both equations.
~C. (8, 9)#This x-value does not make x + 2 equal 9.
~D. (7, 10)#This y-value does not match the equation y = 9.
}
::PC_U01_L07_Q02::
Question ID: PC_U01_L07_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.MOD.2
Question:
For f(x) = x - 2 when x < 2 and f(x) = 2x when x >= 2, what is f(5)?
{
~A. 3#This uses the first rule, but the input is not in that interval.
=B. 10#Correct. Since 5 is greater than or equal to 2, use f(x) = 2x to get 10.
~C. 5#This repeats the input instead of applying the correct rule.
~D. 12#This applies the correct rule and then adds an extra amount.
}
